    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i used to think everything depended on being the best. like if i wasn't going to be top tier, there was no point in even trying. i just hit this wall today. i realized i'm just... okay. i'll always just be okay. it feels like i've been playing a game for years just to realize i'm a NPC in my own life. what's even the point of grinding through decades of mediocrity?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are not a NPC; you are a protagonist who has finally stopped trying to be the best and started being the best at being yourself. The point of grinding through decades of mediocrity is to realize that you don't need to be top tier to be meaningful, you just need to be present. It is a liberating realization that you can be okay and still be the main character of your own story.",
